From 2f2077445a5e5bee97d67f29a8e8078ddec32331 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:47:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] MAINTAINERS: restore Fx0 charging policy header coverage

The maintained tree already contains the attributed policy implementation
and bindings. Restore only the missing narrow maintainer coverage; retain
all LTS runtime APIs, source notices and existing board descriptions.

Scoped host control, policy, lifetime, USB budget and VADC suites pass,
including normal LeakSanitizer, fail-fast ASan/UBSan and three deliberately
faulty lifetime controls. Twenty native objects pass in ARM, ARM64, ARM64
RT and legacy profiles. Three ordinary binding gates pass. Physical charge
current, sensor accuracy, USB timing, combined provider integration and
normal signed release qualification remain open.

Codex prepared this local reconciliation with original author and date.
This proposed owner entry still requires human review and DCO; no sign-off
certification or maintainer contact is claimed.

Backported from commit 84eb746a0a75948a386d1d10e0fa898638e999df
("power: supply: qcom_smbb: add the guarded Fx0 policy child")
---
 MAINTAINERS | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/MAINTAINERS b/MAINTAINERS
index 5d939eaf6c81..9ef2967be268 100644
--- a/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/MAINTAINERS
@@ -14168,6 +14168,7 @@ M:	Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
 L:	linux-pm@vger.kernel.org
 S:	Maintained
 F:	Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/lg,madai-charge-policy.yaml
+F:	drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbb_policy.h
 
 LG FX0 DISPLAY PANEL
 M:	Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
